{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"silly-mystical-annelid","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nThe create sequence must survive process restart without duplicate Jira issues, preserve index-lag grace, and release dependent links/children only after create and binding confirmation are proven.\n\n## Outcome\nRun the complete Cloud/DC crash-restart sequence twice, prove exactly one remote issue and one confirmed binding, then make coordinated create authoritative behind one internal family rollback selector.\n\n## Plan\n1. Compose pending, create, containment, confirmation, and RP-02 keyed/keyless recovery across fresh process/store instances.\n2. Preserve keyed recovery with zero search and keyless recovery with both three misses and 3600 seconds; one recovery failure cannot stop unrelated tickets.\n3. Hold create-before-link and parent-before-child dependents until proven create/confirmation; preserve tombstones, filters, and read-only modes.\n4. Venue-gate Cloud/DC verified-fake crash/restart tests, then switch the internal create-family default. Never run legacy and coordinator creates together.\n5. Preserve exact per-ticket tally, logs, known-key safety abort, and rollback by re-observation.\n\n## Testing\nDuplicate probes execute every fault cut twice with fresh state. Dependency and filter tables assert zero early effects and independent continuation.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every Cloud/DC crash-restart fault cut converges to exactly one remote issue and one confirmed forward/reverse binding.\n- [ ] Keyed recovery performs zero search.\n- [ ] Keyless negative search requires both three misses and 3600 seconds.\n- [ ] Per-entry recovery failure does not stop unrelated tickets.\n- [ ] Links and children wait for proven create/confirmation, while tombstones, filters, and read-only modes remain effective.\n- [ ] Create has one coordinator route and one internal legacy rollback value with no dual-send.\n\n## Out of scope\nFinal removal of legacy create helpers remains S5.","id":"2863-c335-4567-4430","parent_id":"59b0-d1b9-ad94-4339","priority":1,"tags":["rp03","create","recovery","tdd"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"RP-03 S4 T3 — Prove restart convergence and cut over create coordination"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787028379237708001,"uuid":"7dcbfbef-bfdc-4a2f-9e14-50eff74edc5e"}